WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.972
Idea. Dementia is a group of brain diseases that slowly damage memory and thinking. Alzheimer's disease is the most common kind. In Alzheimer's, clumps of a protein called beta-amyloid build up. These clumps are called plaques. They form in the gaps between neurones, the nerve cells, and later inside them. Beta-amyloid forms because another protein, called APP, is not broken down properly.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:42.709
The first symptom of Alzheimer's is usually short-term memory loss. A symptom is a sign of a disease. Short-term memory holds recent events, like what you did today. Long-term memory holds events from years ago, which have been processed more.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:01:06.267
Method. Step one: find the condition the question names. Each one has its own symptoms. Alzheimer's: memory loss, confusion, problems with speech and language, repeating actions, losing thinking ability, and changes in social behaviour. Later, people also lose control of voluntary muscles, the muscles you move on purpose.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:20.766
Parkinson's disease: a tremor, which means shaking, stiff muscles, slow movement, and poor balance and posture. Speech and handwriting change. It can also bring sleep problems, anxiety and depression.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:42.217
Two mental illnesses. Schizophrenia: hallucinations, which means seeing or hearing things that are not there, and confused thinking. Depression: low mood and a lack of energy. Risk factors make illness more likely: low income, low self-esteem, violence or abuse, and drug or alcohol misuse.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:02:00.193
Step two: if the question says other than memory loss, do not give it. Step three: give one different idea for each mark. Speech problems, confusion and repeated actions count as one group, so give only one of them. Then take a different idea from another group.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:21.574
Step four: for a passage, use the lines given, in your own words. For suggest why, give a sensible reason. Richer countries have more dementia. People live longer, because fewer die young of infectious diseases. Diets also have more saturated fat and processed food, and people may drink more alcohol.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:36.169
Worked example. Now a real exam question. Here is a passage about Alzheimer's disease. Part c asks: state two symptoms of Alzheimer's disease, other than memory loss. Two marks.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:49.601
Memory loss is not allowed, so forgetting things is out too. Now think of other symptoms. They fall into these groups. For symptom one, take difficulty with language, such as finding the right words.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:58.487
For symptom two, take a different group: a gradual loss of control of voluntary muscles. Walking and dressing become hard.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:05.290
Here is the full answer. This answer is by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:19.785
Common mistake. A common mistake is to swap conditions. Tremor is a symptom of Parkinson's, not Alzheimer's. Memory loss belongs to Alzheimer's, not to depression or schizophrenia.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:29.692
Another mistake: two answers that are the same idea. Forgets things and cannot remember score only one mark. Choose two different ideas.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:52.889
Your turn. Mr Khan is 72. His hands shake when he is resting, and his handwriting has become very small. He finds it hard to start walking. His daughter says he sleeps badly and seems anxious. Part a: which disease does he most likely have? Part b: give two other symptoms of this disease that are not described here. Pause here and work it out.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:11.823
Answer. Here is the answer. Part a: Parkinson's disease. Part b: shaking, handwriting, slow movement, sleep and anxiety are already in the passage, so cross them out. Give any two of: stiff muscles, poor balance or posture, changes in speech, or depression.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:27.287
So, every time: find the condition. Cross out anything the question excludes. Give one different idea for each mark. For a passage, use the lines given. For suggest, use age, lifestyle or social reasons.
